{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QCasoratianBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QCasoratianBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.casoratian_ratio_bar_self_reciprocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.casoratian_ratio_bar_self_reciprocal","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QCasoratianBarParity.lean#L102-L112","doc":"**`Field` corollary (literal ratio form).** Over a field, with `q, x ≠ 0`, the\nbar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹, x ↦ x⁻¹` fixes the ratio `casNum/casDen`. Derived from\nthe division-free `casoratian_ratio_bar_invariant` above; a convenience\nrestatement, not the primary result. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.casoratian_ratio_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.casoratian_ratio_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QCasoratianBarParity.lean#L85-L100","doc":"**P-C15 (Lean certificate, division-free `CommRing` form).** The 4₁ order-2\nCasoratian ratio `a₀/a₂ = casNum/casDen` is **invariant** under the fibre bar\ninvolution `q ↦ q⁻¹, x ↦ x⁻¹`, expressed without division as the\ncross-multiplied identity\n\n    casNum qi xi · casDen q x = casNum q x · casDen qi xi.\n\nBoth numerator and denominator scale by the *same* monomial `q³x³` under the\ninvolution (`casNum_reciprocal`, `casDen_reciprocal`), so the shared factor\ncancels. Holds over any commutative ring with `q, x` units. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.casDen_reciprocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.casDen_reciprocal","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QCasoratianBarParity.lean#L74-L83","doc":"**Denominator reciprocity.** Same monomial factor `q³x³` — which is why the\ntwist cancels in the ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.casNum_reciprocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.casNum_reciprocal","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QCasoratianBarParity.lean#L58-L72","doc":"**Numerator reciprocity (division-free, over any `CommRing`).** If `q, x` are\nunits — witnessed by `q·qi = 1`, `x·xi = 1` — then the bar-involved numerator,\nscaled by the monomial `q³x³`, returns the numerator:\n\n    casNum qi xi · (q³x³) = casNum q x.\n\n(Exact `linear_combination` certificate; no field, no `field_simp`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.casDen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.casDen","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QCasoratianBarParity.lean#L55-L56","doc":"Denominator of the ratio: `q³x³ − q²x − qx² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.casNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.casNum","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QCasoratianBarParity.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Numerator of the 4₁ order-2 qZeilberger Casoratian ratio `a₀/a₂`\n(with `x = q^N`): `q³x³ − q³x² − x + 1`. Over a generic commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}